    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.21.24",
   "range": "LUK.21.24",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "0bda6840",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.21.24#p1-0bda6840",
     "text": "The Gentiles then shall not always tread down Jerusalem. Those kings of the East, the Jews, may, likely, have their way prepared to it, through Euphrates, Rev 16:12, and Jerusalem be again inhabited by them, even in Jerusalem, Zec 12:6. But this will be not long before the last day, Luk 21:25.",
     "anchor": "Until the times of the Gentiles",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Rev 16:12",
       "ref": "REV.16.12"
      },
      {
       "text": "Zec 12:6",
       "ref": "ZEC.12.6"
      },
      {
       "text": "Luk 21:25",
       "ref": "LUK.21.25"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.21.25",
   "range": "LUK.21.25",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "0f091176",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.21.25#p1-0f091176",
     "text": "See Mat 24:29; Mar 13:24; 2Pe 3:10.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 24:29",
       "ref": "MAT.24.29"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mar 13:24",
       "ref": "MRK.13.24"
      },
      {
       "text": "2Pe 3:10",
       "ref": "2PE.3.10"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.21.26",
   "range": "LUK.21.26",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "59117e33",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.21.26#p1-59117e33",
     "text": "What marvel though wicked men be dispirited, and even ring their bells backwards, when they shall see all on a light fire? Moses himself may tremble at the terror of the mount, and Abraham show some trepidation in such a fright.",
     "anchor": "Men’s hearts failing them"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.21.27",
   "range": "LUK.21.27",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "b80534c2",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.21.27#p1-b80534c2",
     "text": "As on a chariot. See Rev 1:7.",
     "anchor": "Coming in a cloud",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Rev 1:7",
       "ref": "REV.1.7"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.21.28",
   "range": "LUK.21.28",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "e30cc7b1",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.21.28#p1-e30cc7b1",
     "text": "You that shall then be found alive shall soon be caught up, 1Th 4:14-18, and fully freed from all evils and enemies.",
     "anchor": "Look up",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Th 4:14-18",
       "ref": "1TH.4.14-18"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.21.29",
   "range": "LUK.21.29",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "c26b7f72",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.21.29#p1-c26b7f72",
     "text": "See Mat 24:32; Mar 13:28;",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 24:32",
       "ref": "MAT.24.32"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mar 13:28",
       "ref": "MRK.13.28"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.21.30",
   "range": "LUK.21.30",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "c66e32f7",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.21.30#p1-c66e32f7",
     "text": "See Mat 5:18.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 5:18",
       "ref": "MAT.5.18"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.21.34",
   "range": "LUK.21.34",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "d4c6b0d3",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.21.34#p1-d4c6b0d3",
     "text": "The disciples themselves had in them the common poison of nature, and so were obnoxious even to the most reproachful evils. That, πανσπερμια, if watered with the temptation of Satan, what sin may it not produce in the best, unless God prevent? Let the best take heed that they be not irregulares gulares, making the corpse a cloak bag, the gut a gulf, &c. A full belly makes a foul heart: the rankest weeds grow out of the fattest soil.",
     "anchor": "Take heed that your hearts"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.21.35",
   "range": "LUK.21.35",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "88fc24b9",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.21.35#p1-88fc24b9",
     "text": "See Ecc 9:12. {See Trapp on \"Ecc 9:12\"}",
     "anchor": "As a snare",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Ecc 9:12",
       "ref": "ECC.9.12"
      },
      {
       "text": "Ecc 9:12",
       "ref": "ECC.9.12"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.21.36",
   "range": "LUK.21.36",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "8127862d",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.21.36#p1-8127862d",
     "text": "Great is the emphasis of this word, καταξιωθητε (saith learned Beza), for it gives us to understand that we owe all to the free election of God, who loved us first, and so accepted us for worthy, Rev 3:4.",
     "anchor": "That ye may be accounted worthy",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Rev 3:4",
       "ref": "REV.3.4"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.21.37",
   "range": "LUK.21.37",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "cc9cc174",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.21.37#p1-cc9cc174",
     "text": "So he divided his time between preaching and praying; as did also his apostles, Act 6:4. {See Trapp on \"Act 6:4\"}",
     "anchor": "And in the day",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Act 6:4",
       "ref": "ACT.6.4"
      },
      {
       "text": "Act 6:4",
       "ref": "ACT.6.4"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.21.38",
   "range": "LUK.21.38",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "2e77711b",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.21.38#p1-2e77711b",
     "text": "Mancabat, saith the Vulgate, imitating the Greek, ωρθριζε. Let our people look upon their forwardliness, and be ashamed of their long lying, tardy coming to hear the word.",
     "anchor": "Came early in the morning"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
